# =============================================================================
# Project: <YOUR PROJECT NAME>
#
# This file (Yuan.md) is the agent's project-level memory.
# It is loaded into the system prompt on every request.
#
# Sections YuanCode understands out of the box:
#   ## Stack          — languages, runtimes, package managers
#   ## Conventions    — code style, file layout, naming
#   ## Build / Test   — exact commands the agent should run
#   ## Architecture   — high-level module boundaries
#   ## Domain         — business rules the agent must respect
#
# Anything you write here is treated as authoritative guidance.
# Use `Yuan.local.md` (gitignored) for personal overrides.
# =============================================================================

## Stack
- TypeScript 5.7+
- Node.js ≥ 20.10
- Package manager: pnpm 10
- Test framework: vitest

## Conventions
- All public exports must be typed (no `any`).
- Prefer named exports; default exports only for React components.
- Path alias: `@/` → `./src/`.
- Tests must live next to the file they test (`foo.ts` ↔ `foo.test.ts`).
- Never commit secrets; use `.env` (which is gitignored).

## Build / Test
- Install:    `pnpm install`
- Build:      `pnpm build`
- Test:       `pnpm test`
- Lint:       `pnpm lint`
- Typecheck:  `pnpm typecheck`

## Architecture
<!-- Describe the high-level module boundaries here. -->
- `src/core/` — Harness core (AgentLoop, ToolRegistry, PermissionGate, …)
- `src/tools/` — Built-in tools registered with the ToolRegistry
- `src/extensions/` — Yuan.md / Skills / MCP / Hooks loaders
- `src/model/` — Provider adapters (Anthropic / OpenAI / MiniMax / custom)
- `src/cli/` — CLI command implementations
- `src/tui/` — Ink-based terminal UI

## Domain
<!-- Domain-specific rules the agent must follow. -->
- TBD: replace with project-specific business rules.

## Things the agent must NOT do
- Never edit files under `node_modules/`, `dist/`, or `.yuancode/`.
- Never `rm -rf` outside the project root without explicit user confirmation.
- Never push to a remote git without a clear user instruction.
